enn|n|One who is united with others in a league; a person or a nation engaged in a confederacy; an ally; also, an accomplice in a bad sense. ; A name designating an adherent to the cause of the States which attempted to withdraw from the Union (1860-1865).	N:s02,78,1~s02,78,1
enn|a|United in a league; allied by treaty; engaged in a confederacy; banded together; allied. ; Of or pertaining to the government of the eleven Southern States of the United States which (1860-1865) attempted to establish an independent nation styled the Confederate States of America; as, the Confederate congress; Confederate money.	j:s02,93,3~s02,93,3
