fr1|n|An obsolete rude reed instrument (Ger. Zinken), of the oboe family. ; A brass instrument, with cupped mouthpiece, and furnished with valves or pistons, now used in bands, and, in place of the trumpet, in orchestras. See Cornet-a-piston. ; A certain organ stop or register. ; A cap of paper twisted at the end, used by retailers to inclose small wares. ; A troop of cavalry; -- so called from its being accompanied by a cornet player. ; The standard of such a troop. ; The lowest grade of commissioned officer in a British cavalry troop, who carried the standard. The office was abolished in 1871. ; A headdress ; A square cap anciently worn as a mark of certain professions. ; A part of a woman's headdress, in the 16th century. ; See Coronet, 2.	a:1qmx,58,4~1qmx,58,4	n:cdu,139,3~cdu,139,3
